From: "Asrbek (via Claude)" <asrbekshokirovich@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 15:50:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(crm): add /crm/admin/uni-db-review reviewer queue
 (Phase 3R-A)

Wires the React staff CRM into the uni_db HITL queue so Asrbek (or any
profiles.role IN ('uni_db_reviewer','admin','uni_db_admin') user) can
work the review queue without leaving the CRM.

New files
- src/hooks/useUniDbReviewer.ts - reads profiles.role for the current
  auth user. Coexists with the existing useUserRole() (which reads the
  user_roles app_role ENUM); see hanguk-uz-staff-crm-architecture.md
  for why we have two role systems.
- src/hooks/useReviewQueue.ts - react-query wrappers around
  v_review_queue_dashboard plus the three RPC mutations (fn_review_accept,
  fn_review_edit_accept, fn_review_reject). Refetches every 60s.
- src/components/crm/pages/UniDbReviewContent.tsx - the page.
  - Forbidden card if not a reviewer.
  - 4-card stats header (open, overdue, P1+P2, avg confidence).
  - 2-column grid of queue items with priority badges, SLA-overdue
    indicator, source URL, expandable JSON payload, and three actions:
    Accept (with confirm dialog), Edit & Accept (JSON editor dialog),
    Reject (reason-code dropdown matching reviewer-onboarding.md \xc2\xa76).

Modified
- src/components/crm/CRMSidebar.tsx - extracts groups into a buildGroups
  helper to deduplicate the prior copy-paste between the inline groups
  and the exported useSidebarGroups hook. Adds an isUniDbReviewer prop
  + 'Uni DB Review' item under the Admin group, gated on that flag.
- src/pages/CRMPortal.tsx - imports useUniDbReviewer, threads the flag
  to <CRMSidebar> and useSidebarGroups, adds /crm/admin/uni-db-review
  URL prefix recognition + 'uni-db-review' renderContent case with
  lazy-imported UniDbReviewContent.

Companion DB migration (already applied to staging+prod)
- supabase/migrations/20260701001000_uni_db_v3_review_action_rpcs.sql
  in the hanguk_app repo. Defines fn_review_accept / _edit_accept /
  _reject as SECURITY DEFINER plpgsql, plus a reviewer SELECT policy
  on review_queue (the prior RLS only allowed admin SELECT, which
  would have made v_review_queue_dashboard return empty for the
  reviewer role). The trg_review_queue_audit trigger from Phase 1
  still handles the immutable review_decisions audit-log insert when
  status transitions.

Verification still pending
- Visual smoke test on Vercel preview before merge to main.
- npm install / vite build kept timing out in the build sandbox so the
  TypeScript types weren't validated locally; relying on Vercel
  preview to catch any compile errors.
